# Alchemy card narrative game

Unity 6, UGUI, TextMeshPro, New Input System. Narrative card game, not combat.

- Edit the existing scene, prefabs, and scripts. Do not build a second UI.
- Never change Canvas scale.
- Type names: EventPanel, HandTray, CardSlot, EventData. Never Rite, HandCardsController, SimpleDragable.
- Content lives in ScriptableObjects. No hardcoded copy, cards, slots, or requirements.
- Compare card types by typeId, never by display name.
- UI hit tests use EventSystem.RaycastAll, never IsPointerOverGameObject.
- Event text is locked: open shows opening text only; after a card is placed, opening text plus one outcome preview. No scrolling log on the event page.
- Work only on the named phase. Do not pull in later phases.
- If a requirement is ambiguous, ask before creating a new script.
- Prefer editing existing files. Touch about three files per task unless the task names more.

Phase order (P0–P10), one at a time, tag before the next:

0. Verify current event loop (open → slot filter → drag → preview → confirm/cancel). Tag `phase1-loop`.
1. SpringMotion / MotionSettings liquid feel on hand, drag tilt, dock, panel, tags.
2. AttributeCatalog + card/event attribute lists; fine type tags; stackable/equip/food fields; ID validator.
3. Deck vs hand split (CardInstance, GameState, DeckConfig). Tag after verify.
4. Hand card face (attrs + count) + flat fine HandCardTag bar + slot filter.
5. Requirement diff panel (threshold tiers, Attribute prefab rows).
6. Confirm runs settlements (SerializeReference conditions/commands). Cancel changes nothing. Tag `phase3-settle`.
7. CardInformation: character eat/equip, effective attrs.
8. Switches, variables, rounds, common events. Tag `phase4-events`.
9. RPG Maker-like event editor window.
10. Alchemy as event asset (recipe quality + GrantRecipeOutput).

Alchemy brewing is a later event asset (recipe, herbs, tool, character), not a new system before P6. Tags and a card-id validator are data-foundation (P2), not part of hand layout.
